to their homeland want us still!

190
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:24,820
How can I face them in defeat?

191
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:40,857
To think that I trusted
you with their memories,

192
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:43,237
their cries for
revenge—that have echoed for

193
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:46,277
three centuries—I can
hardly live with myself.

194
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:47,190
with myself

195
