255
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:19,080
A while ago, deep beneath the sea...

256
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:28,917
Luffy and the Straw Hats had just
saved the Ryugu Kingdom from the new

257
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:33,235
Fishman Pirates and received the
Tomate Box from King Neptune as thanks.

258
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:36,390
However...

259
00:19:36,473 --> 00:19:37,303
Please, Your Majesty!

260
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:39,677
I'm not sure if Luffy
and the others found the

261
00:19:39,760 --> 00:19:42,936
Tomate Box among the stolen
treasures we gave to them,

262
00:19:43,260 --> 00:19:47,537
but, uh, it might be wise to ask them
to give that particular present back!

263
00:19:47,620 --> 00:19:48,796
What are you saying?

264
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:53,315
I could never ask them to return a
gift that we gave them for saving us.

265
00:19:53,420 --> 00:19:56,360
The problem is it's not exactly treasure.

266
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:59,300
It's more like a bomb, actually.

267
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:00,650
What?

268
00:20:00,733 --> 00:20:02,800
It'll explode if they open it?

269
00:20:02,980 --> 00:20:05,392
I must ask them to return it immediately.

270
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:10,440
You gave the treasure away?

271
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:12,520
And the big mom no less?

272
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:16,159
Well, maybe the explosives
are no longer functional.

273
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,777
Very good, Your Majesty.

274
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:20,100
Misty, I do admire your positivity.

275
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:24,800
And now, back to the present.

276
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:30,557
This is the Red Bean Bomb meeting room.

277
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:34,257
We've got a massive crack running
from the Eastern Bomb second floor.

278
00:20:34,340 --> 00:20:37,280
Not just a crack, it's
split straight in half.

279
00:20:37,860 --> 00:20:39,684
Red Bean Bomb third floor here.

280
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:41,100
What is going on?

281
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:44,046
You don't think this is
an earthquake, do you?

282
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:46,180
We're gonna topple over!

283
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:48,070
Damn it!

284
00:20:48,153 --> 00:20:50,137
I swear I heard an explosion before this!

285
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:51,437
So it's an enemy attack!

286
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:52,350
Doesn't matter!

287
00:20:52,433 --> 00:20:53,263
Let's get going!

288
00:20:53,346 --> 00:20:54,888
Whoever did this will help!

289
00:21:20,380 --> 00:21:21,640
Who wasn't the enemy?

290
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:23,700
Maybe, but I don't know how.

291
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:26,280
Who could invade an emperor's home base?

292
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:28,678
They must have snuck in with a bomb.

293
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:34,357
Ridiculous, and how the hell
did they get away with it?

294
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:35,900
Please don't follow us.

295
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:37,747
I'm going to die, aren't we?

296
00:21:37,940 --> 00:21:41,646
Does this have something to do
with the wedding on the rooftop?

297
00:21:57,900 --> 00:22:03,440
This is a total nightmare,
but it's also big news.

298
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:12,217
Was there a bomb in
that box, probably yes?

299
00:22:12,300 --> 00:22:15,137
The timing was dead on.

300
00:22:15,220 --> 00:22:18,937
I don't know what else could
have caused it, but why?

301
00:22:19,020 --> 00:22:21,440
Surely they couldn't have planned this.

302
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:25,757
We're going down.

303
00:22:25,840 --> 00:22:26,800
Hold on tight.

304
00:22:28,980 --> 00:22:30,660
I lost track of the enemy.

305
00:22:31,960 --> 00:22:33,937
Did one of your allies do this?

306
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:37,797
Beats me, all I know is
that if this didn't happen,

307
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:40,140
then all of us would be dead for sure.

308
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:47,600
What was that noise?

309
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:49,547
What happened to my Shit?

310
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:04,440
Something or other saved us.

311
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:07,480
I wouldn't say we're saved just yet.

312
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:10,960
Far from it, in fact!

313
00:23:12,020 --> 00:23:13,940
We're in big trouble, Mama!

314
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:15,720
We don't know where,

315
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:19,677
but an explosion went off and
now the whole Shit is collapsing.

316
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:20,820
We're going down!

317
00:23:33,840 --> 00:23:35,517
Something's going on out there.

318
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:38,897
It's kind of weird how we can't
feel anything inside, Beach, huh?

319
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:41,156
Any idea what might have caused this?

320
00:23:42,680 --> 00:23:43,680
I don't know.

321
00:23:43,940 --> 00:23:45,480
But it's clear.

322
00:23:45,860 --> 00:23:48,720
The situation has devolved into chaos.

323
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:52,220
Judging from what I can see,

324
00:23:52,480 --> 00:23:55,833
it seems that the Shit itself
is toppling on its side.

325
00:23:56,380 --> 00:23:58,560
What kind of joke is this?

326
00:23:58,760 --> 00:24:00,097
What do you mean, joke?

327
00:24:00,180 --> 00:24:01,180
It's a nightmare.

328
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:05,080
Damn, see that?

329
00:24:07,140 --> 00:24:09,340
This is a good thing, right?

330
00:24:12,180 --> 00:24:14,340
Who did this?

331
00:24:15,260 --> 00:24:18,000
How is this even possible?

332
00:24:18,700 --> 00:24:20,100
My brothers.

333
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:21,860
My sisters.

334
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:25,100
Are they gonna be okay?

335
00:24:27,960 --> 00:24:30,160
I guess so!

336
00:24:30,720 --> 00:24:31,550
Mama!

337
00:24:44,620 --> 00:24:45,450
No!

338
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:49,190
No!

339
00:25:02,980 --> 00:25:04,160
This is rich.

340
00:25:05,060 --> 00:25:09,257
I don't know who to thank for this, but
they knocked it out of the ballpark.

341
00:25:09,340 --> 00:25:12,957
i don't even gotta knock
off big mom anymore what's

342
00:25:13,040 --> 00:25:17,780
the point look at them the
big mom pirates are Toast!

343
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:19,240
They're done for!

344
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:29,120
As good as dead!

345
00:25:37,740 --> 00:25:40,152
The castle is bigger than the whole city!

346
00:25:40,300 --> 00:25:42,137
It doesn't matter if you run or not!

347
00:25:42,220 --> 00:25:44,279
None of us are making it out alive!

348
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:56,560
Big brother!

349
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:01,400
Let's stay calm.

350
00:26:04,720 --> 00:26:07,320
This is big news! Really big!

351
00:26:07,880 --> 00:26:08,710
Yeah!

352
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:11,477
At this rate, you'll take it to the grave.

353
00:26:11,560 --> 00:26:12,390
All right!

354
00:26:12,473 --> 00:26:13,303
I can't fly!

355
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:19,830
Unreal.

356
00:26:20,800 --> 00:26:25,680
If we really are witnessing the end of
the Big Mom Pirates, Morgan's is right.

357
00:26:26,920 --> 00:26:28,520
That's quite a scoop.

358
00:26:38,600 --> 00:26:39,430
Hey!

359
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:41,680
Come up here, hurry!

360
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:44,580
This way!

361
00:26:44,780 --> 00:26:46,257
I think you'd better hurry!

362
00:26:46,340 --> 00:26:48,140
He's got boofy, too!

363
00:26:49,840 --> 00:26:51,900
I figured you were both both.

364
00:26:53,900 --> 00:26:55,429
Sorry to keep you waiting.

365
00:26:55,520 --> 00:26:56,579
You two are crazy.

366
00:26:56,820 --> 00:26:58,291
I hope that was worth it.

367
00:26:58,380 --> 00:27:00,027
We're glad that you're back.

368
00:27:01,140 --> 00:27:03,860
Okay, Caesar, let's amskrain.

369
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:06,137
What, did you think I was going back?

370
00:27:06,220 --> 00:27:08,060
So long, suckers!

371
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:11,680
I think they're good.

372
00:27:13,620 --> 00:27:14,680
Mission complete.

373
00:27:14,900 --> 00:27:15,730
Let's withdraw.

374
00:27:15,813 --> 00:27:17,040
We're on our way.

375
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:50,160
Hey, are you all right, pal?

376
00:27:53,840 --> 00:27:55,460
It's too late!

377
00:27:55,760 --> 00:27:57,620
We're done for!

378
00:27:59,740 --> 00:28:00,740
Formatamorphosis!

379
00:28:01,980 --> 00:28:02,860
Giant!

380
00:28:20,680 --> 00:28:30,920
SCREAMING.

381
00:28:47,220 --> 00:28:48,537
That

382
00:28:48,620 --> 00:28:49,937
was

383
00:28:50,020 --> 00:28:56,220
a close one.

384
00:29:06,640 --> 00:29:08,080
Some kind of cream.

385
00:29:15,060 --> 00:29:16,157
What the hell!

386
00:29:16,240 --> 00:29:17,580
It's sponge cave.

387
00:29:30,920 --> 00:29:32,620
What the hell was that?

388
00:29:35,120 --> 00:29:37,260
The whole cake Shit.

389
00:29:37,560 --> 00:29:39,820
It turned into an actual cake.

390
00:29:40,260 --> 00:29:41,100
Nice move.

391
00:29:41,640 --> 00:29:44,437
All this was the head
chef's work, I would guess.

392
00:29:44,520 --> 00:29:46,932
Save the entire family in one fell swoop.

393
00:29:50,880 --> 00:29:52,760
Mama, are you okay?

394
00:29:53,680 --> 00:29:54,700
A cake.

395
00:29:55,300 --> 00:29:57,920
My castle turned into a cake.

396
00:30:01,360 --> 00:30:02,780
Ah, I forgot.

397
00:30:03,260 --> 00:30:07,237
The sweets that Struzan makes with
his ability may fill your stomach,

398
00:30:07,320 --> 00:30:09,840
but don't taste very good. You made it!

399
00:30:12,320 --> 00:30:13,500
I was worried.

400
00:30:13,800 --> 00:30:14,680
What a mess.

401
00:30:16,240 --> 00:30:17,440
Little rats.

402
00:30:17,700 --> 00:30:20,420
Those bastards ruined my wedding cake.

403
00:30:22,800 --> 00:30:24,000
My cake.

404
00:30:28,020 --> 00:30:29,080
Easy does it.

405
00:30:29,500 --> 00:30:31,440
Can I get a hand here? Come on.

406
00:30:31,740 --> 00:30:33,152
Everything will be fine.

407
00:30:33,560 --> 00:30:35,325
I thought I was gone for sure.

408
00:30:35,740 --> 00:30:37,580
I mean, crush my cake!

409
00:30:38,080 --> 00:30:40,433
I heard someone yelling from over there!

410
00:30:40,680 --> 00:30:41,856
Hurry and help them!

411
00:30:42,540 --> 00:30:43,370
Come on.

412
00:30:44,820 --> 00:30:45,940
Look who's here!

413
00:30:46,380 --> 00:30:48,180
Mondore, sir! What happened?

414
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:51,897
Why did the whole cake
Shit collapse like that?

415
00:30:51,980 --> 00:30:53,777
The entire city got wrecked!

416
00:30:53,860 --> 00:30:55,377
And what's with all this heavy cream?

417
00:30:55,460 --> 00:30:56,520
Shut your traps!

418
00:30:57,080 --> 00:30:58,897
This is not over yet!

419
00:30:58,980 --> 00:31:02,920
Our enemies who plotted to
assassinate mama have gotten away.

420
00:31:03,320 --> 00:31:06,780
We lost their trail, but they
couldn't have gone very far

421
00:31:07,600 --> 00:31:10,657
Hurry and call the tarts
on all total land islands.

422
00:31:10,740 --> 00:31:15,197
We're looking for the Straw Hat pirates
and the fire tank pirates as well.

423
00:31:15,280 --> 00:31:18,360
Don't let a single one of them escape!

424
00:31:19,620 --> 00:31:20,450
I.

425
00:31:25,420 --> 00:31:27,677
Think this is far enough—get out!

426
00:31:27,760 --> 00:31:28,590
out

427
00:31:36,940 --> 00:31:38,637
Thanks for everything, Veggie.

428
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:40,637
We might be dead if it wasn't for you.

429
00:31:40,720 --> 00:31:44,100
Don't get sappy on me like
I'd ever do a good deed.

430
00:31:44,740 --> 00:31:45,570
Disgusting.

431
00:31:45,940 --> 00:31:48,277
If you're gonna thank
someone, then thank me!

432
00:31:48,360 --> 00:31:49,480
I care with you!

433
00:31:49,920 --> 00:31:51,080
Can it, you loser!

434
00:31:51,520 --> 00:31:55,697
You know, I haven't forgotten what
you did to those kids on Punk Hazard.

435
00:31:55,780 --> 00:31:57,757
We do not need your help anymore.

436
00:31:57,840 --> 00:32:00,160
So go drop dead. Huh? Ah!

437
00:32:01,100 --> 00:32:02,000
Foolish girl!

438
00:32:02,280 --> 00:32:04,897
You should show respect
when you speak to a genius!

439
00:32:04,980 --> 00:32:08,997
Do you want me to turn this entire
island into a wasteland of poison gas?

440
00:32:09,080 --> 00:32:10,100
Because I will!

441
00:32:10,860 --> 00:32:11,690
Huh?

442
00:32:11,960 --> 00:32:12,790
Here.

443
00:32:12,873 --> 00:32:13,703
Take your heart.

444
00:32:19,660 --> 00:32:21,740
I can't believe it.

445
00:32:21,980 --> 00:32:24,392
I never thought this moment would arrive.

446
00:32:26,740 --> 00:32:29,120
You earned your freedom, you scumbag.

447
00:32:29,320 --> 00:32:30,908
You should have crushed it.

448
00:32:33,060 --> 00:32:33,890
No!

449
00:32:33,973 --> 00:32:35,100
Oh, please, please.

450
00:32:37,840 --> 00:32:39,193
Should have crushed it.

451
00:32:49,480 --> 00:32:50,660
My heart!

452
00:32:51,440 --> 00:32:54,820
I'm finally, finally whole again!

453
00:32:55,940 --> 00:32:57,197
So long, suckers!

454
00:32:57,280 --> 00:32:58,660
I'll see you in hell!

455
00:32:59,860 --> 00:33:00,690
Morons!

456
00:33:00,773 --> 00:33:02,537
Simpletons! Nedwins! Good riddance!

457
00:33:02,620 --> 00:33:03,914
Why'd the castle fall?

458
00:33:04,120 --> 00:33:05,780
Seems kind of sudden, huh?

459
00:33:06,100 --> 00:33:08,217
So, do you Karoo know who caused this?

460
00:33:08,300 --> 00:33:09,700
Not the slightest clue!

461
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:11,840
Pay attention to me, dammit!

462
00:33:12,020 --> 00:33:13,160
Bad news, Father!

463
00:33:14,840 --> 00:33:17,657
Believe it or not, but
the enemy is still alive!

464
00:33:17,740 --> 00:33:20,681
They're a little shaken
up, Lili, but that's all!

465
00:33:20,860 --> 00:33:23,820
The whole Shit turned into a cake, Lili.

466
00:33:24,980 --> 00:33:25,810
Aha.

467
00:33:25,893 --> 00:33:28,027
That would be Strewson's
anti-work, I assume.

468
00:33:29,180 --> 00:33:31,240
That man was a mystery to me.

469
00:33:31,380 --> 00:33:33,145
Who knows what he had cooking.

470
00:33:36,100 --> 00:33:39,480
That is to say, he's
more than just a chef.

471
00:33:39,780 --> 00:33:42,220
He's probably a real tough cookie, too.

472
00:33:44,660 --> 00:33:49,077
I thought the big mom pirates were
kaput after seeing the Shit collapse.

473
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:51,140
They're lucky to have that guy.

474
00:33:51,480 --> 00:33:52,760
But that's fine.

475
00:33:52,960 --> 00:33:54,313
They still got screwed.

476
00:33:54,980 --> 00:33:56,745
But that makes me feel better.

477
00:33:56,900 --> 00:33:59,200
Would somebody please validate me?

478
00:33:59,640 --> 00:34:01,580
So now we just gotta run away?

479
00:34:01,980 --> 00:34:03,880
Kid, we've been trying to run.

480
00:34:04,080 --> 00:34:06,037
It's just that people
keep getting in our way.

481
00:34:06,120 --> 00:34:07,120
They're gone now.

482
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:08,500
But let's hurry.

483
00:34:08,860 --> 00:34:11,720
Do as you like, but we're
parting ways. Adios.

484
00:34:12,400 --> 00:34:13,400
Oh, really?

485
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:15,997
We failed to assassinate Big Mom.

486
00:34:16,080 --> 00:34:19,137
We have no reason to
continue with this alliance.

487
00:34:19,220 --> 00:34:24,617
This guy gets it, but just as a tip:
I'd start hauling ass if I were you,

488
00:34:24,700 --> 00:34:28,597
even after you set sail—it'll take a whole
day to get out of Big Mom's territory.

489
00:34:28,680 --> 00:34:29,797
True enough.

490
00:34:29,880 --> 00:34:35,457
Good luck, you bunch
of wackos, castle tank!

491
00:34:35,540 --> 00:34:36,370
tank

492
00:34:44,120 --> 00:34:46,000
The Straw Hats went that way?

493
00:34:46,440 --> 00:34:49,020
Come on, how petty can that bastard get?

494
00:34:49,180 --> 00:34:50,100
Shove it, pal.

495
00:34:50,340 --> 00:34:52,480
I gotta survive. No fair!

496
00:34:52,940 --> 00:34:55,677
I wanted to give them a
proper farewell le long.

497
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:58,584
Nami's my friend and we
took off without a word.

498
00:34:58,820 --> 00:34:59,657
Complain later.

499
00:34:59,740 --> 00:35:02,100
Being clear, things might get rough.

500
00:35:03,240 --> 00:35:05,122
Well, guess we'll be on our way.

501
00:35:05,300 --> 00:35:07,277
After retrieving the shark submerged,

502
00:35:07,360 --> 00:35:10,057
we'll take it straight to the
sun and meet up with you there.

503
00:35:10,140 --> 00:35:11,680
Okay, be careful.

504
00:35:12,440 --> 00:35:16,087
We gotta make it all the way to
the coast, so we better hurry.

505
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:19,500
Daifugo, form two attack units.

506
00:35:20,200 --> 00:35:21,120
You got it.

507
00:35:21,740 --> 00:35:23,040
Soldiers, split up.

508
00:35:23,200 --> 00:35:24,906
We're chasing down the enemy.

509
00:35:25,800 --> 00:35:27,660
Half of you go after Straw Hat,

510
00:35:27,860 --> 00:35:31,017
and the other half will bring
back the head of that traitor,

511
00:35:31,100 --> 00:35:31,930
Buggy.

512
00:35:37,500 --> 00:35:38,800
Mama, listen!

513
00:35:41,380 --> 00:35:42,900
They won't escape.

514
00:35:43,160 --> 00:35:45,160
Don't worry, they'll pay for this.

515
00:35:45,620 --> 00:35:46,900
My cake.

516
00:35:48,840 --> 00:35:53,960
It had the best ingredients,
carefully selected.

517
00:35:54,380 --> 00:35:57,080
It was going to be the queen of all cakes.

518
00:35:57,540 --> 00:36:01,060
This was supposed to be the perfect day.

519
00:36:07,320 --> 00:36:12,380
Give me my wedding cake right now.

520
00:36:13,440 --> 00:36:14,657
Oh no!

521
00:36:14,740 --> 00:36:21,540
Where is my cake?

522
00:36:22,320 --> 00:36:25,000
Why are you hiding my
wedding cake from me?

523
00:36:26,140 --> 00:36:27,997
Please, not now, Mama.

524
00:36:28,080 --> 00:36:30,737
Bring me my wedding cake.

525
00:36:30,820 --> 00:36:33,580
Give it to me now!
